-- title:
--   Second-branch value of f/x^m at a supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\overline{\alpha}, \overline{\beta}$ in level $N\cdot q$, a place specialisation $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$, with $k$ perfect; let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$, $c$ a system of node coordinates $x,y$ in the ring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ (so $x$ has vanishing first-branch residue and second-branch residue of order $1$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \bullet w$, and symmetrically for $y$), and $\varpi$ an element of $A \cap K$. Assume the node ring is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal spanned by the constant $\varpi$ together with $x$ and $y$; that every element of it differs from some constant by a non-unit; that $\mathrm{redRestrict}\ \mathrm{red}\ K\ d = 0$ exactly for the multiples of $\varpi$; the value integrality law for $w$ (places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ reducing to $w$ evaluate node integers into $A$); and that $w$ is a supersingular place. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ an irreducible element of $W$, $E \geq 1$, and $\iota$ a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the node ring onto the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^{E})$; let $\mathrm{wmap} : A \cap K \to W$ send $\varpi$ to $\pi$ and be compatible with $\iota$ on constants, and $\rho : W \to k$ satisfy $\rho \circ \mathrm{wmap} = \mathrm{redRestrict}\ \mathrm{red}\ K$. Assume further: a place $V_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V_0 = w$; the compatibility law that for every node integer $g$ and every place $V$ over $w$, the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \bullet w$ takes at the second-branch residue of $g$ the value $\mathrm{red}(V.\mathrm{evalAt}\ g)$; units $\alpha_U, \beta_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota(\hat{x}) = U\alpha_U$ and $\iota(\hat{y}) = V\beta_V$, and a power series $G_\alpha$ representing $\alpha_U$. Finally let $f$ be a node integer whose second-branch residue is non-zero and has order $m \in \mathbb{N}$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \bullet w$, and let $\gamma$ be a unit of the crossing model, represented by a power series $G_\gamma$, with $\iota(\hat{f}) - \gamma U^{m}$ in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and by $V$. Then the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \bullet w$ takes at the quotient of the second-branch residue of $f$ by the $m$-th power of the second-branch residue of $x$ the value $\rho(G_\gamma(0))\cdot \rho(G_\alpha(0))^{-m}$, in the sense that this quotient lies in the valuation subring of that place and its residue is the image of that element of $k$.
--
--   This is the final reading step in the analysis of a supersingular crossing of the special fibre: once the completed local ring at the node has been identified with the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$ and the coordinates $x,y$ with $U,V$ up to units, the value of a ratio $f/x^{m}$ along the second branch is computed from the constant terms of representing power series through the residue map $\rho : W \to k$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_residueFst_div_pow_and_residueSnd_div_pow_and_div_eq_angFactor_of_inertiaStable`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_residueFst_div_pow_and_residueSnd_div_pow_and_div_eq_angFactor_of_inertiaStable), where the two branch readings are combined into the angular factor attached to the node.
